'''Acaridæ''' (a-kar′i-dē), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''Acarus'' + ''-idæ''.] A family of the order ''Acarida'' (which see), including the true mites, as the cheese-mite, ''Acarus domesticus''. See ''Acarus'' and ''cheese-mite''.

'''acaridan''' (a-kar′i-dan), ''a.'' and ''n.'' '''I.''' ''a.'' Of or belonging to the ''Acarida'' or ''Acaridæ''.

'''II.''' ''n.'' One of the ''Acarida''.
